    234  636d							; ------------------------------------------------------------ One Key Play
    235  636d							; CRSR DOWN or CRSR RIGHT (A = 1 / 2: which) pressed, ONE KEY PLAY on: the
    236  636d							; phrase's next step sounds. PENTATONIC PAIRS: two notes of the key's
    237  636d							; pentatonic scale, one apart (a third or a fourth), across the overlay's two
    238  636d							; octaves. CHORD NOTES: one note of the chord (the keys held or latched),
    239  636d							; over two octaves. EACH PRESS CUTS the last step or lets it RING ON (until
    240  636d							; the next). The notes sound while either key is down (latch: until the next
    241  636d							; press).
    242  636d				   OkpPress
    243  636d					      subroutine
    244  636d		       0d 79 c8 	      ora	okpDown
    245  6370		       8d 79 c8 	      sta	okpDown
